 212:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c **** /**
 213:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   * @brief  Update SystemCoreClock variable according to Clock Register Values.
 214:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *         The SystemCoreClock variable contains the core clock (HCLK), it can
 215:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *         be used by the user application to setup the SysTick timer or configure
 216:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *         other parameters.
 217:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 218:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   * @note   Each time the core clock (HCLK) changes, this function must be called
 219:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *         to update SystemCoreClock variable value. Otherwise, any configuration
 220:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *         based on this variable will be incorrect.
 221:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 222:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   * @note   - The system frequency computed by this function is not the real
 223:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *           frequency in the chip. It is calculated based on the predefined
 224:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *           constant and the selected clock source:
 225:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 226:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is MSI, SystemCoreClock will contain the MSI_VALUE(*)
 227:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 228:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSI, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSI_VALUE(**)
 229:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 230:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSE, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(***)
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccGzrbzo.s 			page 6


 231:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 232:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is PLL, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(***)
 233:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *             or HSI_VALUE(*) or MSI_VALUE(*) multiplied/divided by the PLL factors.
 234:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 235:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *         (*) MSI_VALUE is a constant defined in stm32l4xx_hal.h file (default value
 236:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *             4 MHz) but the real value may vary depending on the variations
 237:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *             in voltage and temperature.
 238:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 239:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *         (**) HSI_VALUE is a constant defined in stm32l4xx_hal.h file (default value
 240:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *              16 MHz) but the real value may vary depending on the variations
 241:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *              in voltage and temperature.
 242:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 243:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *         (***) HSE_VALUE is a constant defined in stm32l4xx_hal.h file (default value
 244:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *              8 MHz), user has to ensure that HSE_VALUE is same as the real
 245:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *              frequency of the crystal used. Otherwise, this function may
 246:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *              have wrong result.
 247:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 248:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *         - The result of this function could be not correct when using fractional
 249:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *           value for HSE crystal.
 250:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   *
 251:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   * @retval None
 252:Core/Src/system_stm32l4xx.c ****   */
